## Exam-day tactics

- Flag and return: don't sink time into one question. Feeling like you're failing midway is normal.
- Name the qualifiers first (edition/tier, default vs maximum, the exact object type) before reading the options.
- Only change an answer if you can name the specific fact that makes the first choice wrong.
- On numbers: when stuck between a round number and an odd one, the round one is often the distractor.
- Answer every question if there's no penalty for wrong answers (check the exam's rules).

